╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ parametrized_entangling_with_shared_output                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz has 146 parameters (96 circuit + 2 readout) and achieves excellent     │
│                          │ accuracy (98% test, 99% validation). However, we can improve parameter efficiency while   │
│                          │ maintaining accuracy by:                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Replacing fixed CZ gates with parametrized CRZ gates**: This adds expressiveness to  │
│                          │ the entangling layer without additional single-qubit overhead. Each CRZ can learn an      │
│                          │ optimal rotation angle rather than being fixed.                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Sharing the final RZ layer across all qubits**: Instead of 8 independent RZ          │
│                          │ parameters post-entanglement, use a single shared parameter. This reduces parameters      │
│                          │ while still allowing per-qubit phase alignment through the RY and pre-entangling RZ       │
│                          │ layers.                                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Removing the pre-CZ RZ layer**: When using parametrized CRZ instead of fixed CZ, the │
│                          │ pre-CZ RZ layer becomes partially redundant. The RY layer already provides single-qubit   │
│                          │ rotation freedom, and the RZ can be post-entangling.                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This reduces parameters per block from 24 to 16 (33% reduction), bringing total circuit   │
│                          │ parameters from 96 to 64 and total parameters from 146 to 66. The parametrized two-qubit  │
│                          │ gates should provide sufficient expressiveness to maintain or improve accuracy while      │
│                          │ dramatically improving parameter efficiency.                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected improvements:                                                                    │
│                          │ - Reduced parameter count (66 vs 146): 55% reduction                                      │
│                          │ - Better parameter efficiency metric                                                      │
│                          │ - Potentially faster convergence                                                          │
│                          │ - Maintained or improved accuracy due to more expressive parametrized gates               │
│                          │ - Reduced circuit depth and gate complexity                                               │
