│ patch_name               │ compact_circular_ansatz                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ The seed ansatz (24 parameters per block) contains functional redundancies: an RZ layer   │
│                          │ followed by a diagonal CZ layer and another RZ layer is mathematically equivalent to an   │
│                          │ RZ-CZ-Identity sequence on each wire, as RZ gates commute with CZ.                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This improvement:                                                                         │
│                          │ 1.  Reduces parameters from 24 to 16 per block by removing the redundant RZ layer.        │
│                          │ 2.  Enhances entanglement by replacing the linear CZ chain with a circular CNOT chain,    │
│                          │ ensuring better information flow between all qubits (0-7 and 7-0) within each block.      │
│                          │ 3.  Improves parameter efficiency (a key component of the combined score) while           │
│                          │ maintaining the expressivity needed to reach high accuracy. Total parameters are reduced  │
│                          │ from 146 to 98.                                                                           │
