│ patch_description        │ The previous best candidate (1.25 score) used a block with three single-qubit rotation    │
│                          │ layers (RY, RZ, RZ) and a linear fixed CZ chain, totaling 24 parameters per block (146    │
│                          │ total).                                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I propose a more expressive entangling strategy while keeping the parameter count         │
│                          │ identical (24 per block, 146 total). This design uses:                                    │
│                          │ 1. An RY layer to create initial superposition.                                           │
│                          │ 2. A circular chain of parametrized CRZ gates (8 gates). Unlike fixed CZ gates, CRZ       │
│                          │ allows the model to learn the optimal entanglement strength between all adjacent qubits   │
│                          │ in a closed ring (0-1-2-3-4-5-6-7-0).                                                     │
│                          │ 3. An RX layer to ensure full Bloch sphere coverage, providing a rotation axis orthogonal │
│                          │ to the previous RY and the subsequent IsingZZ feature map rotations.                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This configuration is expected to improve the model's expressivity and convergence speed  │
│                          │ by allowing finer control over the entanglement between qubits, which is crucial for      │
│                          │ processing the two-qubit IsingZZ feature couplings.                                       │
