│ patch_description        │ The best previous program achieved a combined score of 1.37 with perfect accuracy across  │
│                          │ all sets by using:                                                                        │
│                          │ - Individual RY rotations on all qubits                                                   │
│                          │ - A linear chain of parametrized controlled-Z gates (CRZ)                                 │
│                          │ - A shared final RZ layer (parameter reuse)                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This structure yielded 98 total parameters and excellent generalization.                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current program (score 1.25) uses 146 parameters with a different structure (separate │
│                          │ pre/post RZ layers with fixed CZ gates), which appears to be overparameterized and        │
│                          │ underperforms.                                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I propose testing CRY (parametrized controlled-Y) gates in place of CRZ, maintaining the  │
│                          │ efficient linear chain structure and shared final layer. CRY offers different rotation    │
│                          │ axis expressivity and may provide better learning dynamics while keeping the parameter    │
│                          │ count identical to the best program. This change:                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Reduces parameters from 146 to 98 (matching the best program)                          │
│                          │ 2. Maintains the proven linear entanglement pattern                                       │
│                          │ 3. Explores alternative parametrized two-qubit gate types                                 │
│                          │ 4. Preserves parameter sharing efficiency                                                 │
│                          │ 5. Keeps circuit depth competitive                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The hypothesis is that CRY gates may offer complementary expressivity to CRZ for this     │
│                          │ classification task, while the efficient parameter sharing should help achieve fast       │
│                          │ convergence.                                                                              │
