│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ enhanced_crz_entanglement                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves perfect accuracy (1.00 on all splits) with only 98           │
│                          │ parameters and low depth (93). However, it takes 390 convergence steps, which is higher   │
│                          │ than needed.                                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key observations from prior programs:                                                     │
│                          │ 1. The seed program (98 params, simple RY-CNOT-RZ) achieved 0.99 accuracy in 240 steps    │
│                          │ 2. The second program (146 params, RY-CZ-RY structure) achieved 0.98 accuracy in 180      │
│                          │ steps                                                                                     │
│                          │ 3. The current program (98 params, RY-CRZ-RZ sharing) achieves 1.00 accuracy in 390 steps │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current ansatz uses adjacent-pair CRZ gates only. To improve convergence speed while  │
│                          │ maintaining perfect accuracy, I propose enhancing the entanglement pattern by:            │
│                          │ 1. Keeping the successful 8 independent RY parameters                                     │
│                          │ 2. Expanding CRZ connectivity to include both nearest-neighbor pairs (0-1, 2-3, 4-5, 6-7) │
│                          │ AND cross-layer pairs (1-3, 3-5, 5-7, 7-1)                                                │
│                          │ 3. Maintaining the shared final RZ parameter for efficiency                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This 16-parameter design maintains parameter efficiency while enabling richer             │
│                          │ entanglement patterns that can learn the classification boundary faster. The cross-pair   │
│                          │ entanglement creates longer-range correlations between qubits, helping the circuit        │
│                          │ converge with fewer steps while preserving accuracy.                                      │
