│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ aggressive_parameter_sharing_entangling_layer                                             │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves excellent accuracy (1.0) and low loss (0.07) with 98         │
│                          │ parameters through strategic parameter sharing (the final RZ layer shares one parameter   │
│                          │ across all qubits). However, convergence is slower (300 steps vs 120 in prior variants).  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key insight is that the entangling layer (CRY chain) uses 7 distinct parameters for   │
│                          │ what is fundamentally the same entangling operation pattern along a chain. This suggests  │
│                          │ that these parameters may be over-parameterized relative to the benefit they              │
│                          │ provide—especially since they don't significantly reduce losses (0.07 vs 0.09 in second   │
│                          │ program with 146 params).                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ By collapsing the 7 distinct CRY parameters into a single shared parameter (analogous to  │
│                          │ how the final RZ layer already shares one param), we:                                     │
│                          │ 1. Reduce total circuit parameters from 98 to 62 (6 blocks × 10 params + 2 readout)       │
│                          │ 2. Improve parameter efficiency from 0.01 to ~0.016 (better accuracy/param ratio)         │
│                          │ 3. Simplify the optimization landscape, potentially accelerating convergence              │
│                          │ 4. Maintain the proven effective structure: single-qubit rotations → chain entanglement → │
│                          │ shared final rotation                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This tests the hypothesis that the entangling pattern itself (chain connectivity) matters │
│                          │ more than position-specific parameters.                                                   │
