                         Patch Metadata - Gen 16/20 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ simplify_to_proven_pattern                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz (146 parameters) significantly underperforms the second-ranked program │
│                          │ (98 parameters, score 1.51) despite attempting greater complexity. The current program    │
│                          │ shows:                                                                                    │
│                          │ - 3× worse validation loss (0.10 vs 0.03)                                                 │
│                          │ - 48 extra parameters providing no accuracy benefit                                       │
│                          │ - Slower convergence in loss despite faster epoch convergence                             │
│                          │ - Same test accuracy (1.0) but much higher training instability                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The second-ranked program succeeds with a simpler, lean entanglement structure:           │
│                          │ - Initial RY layer on all qubits (per-qubit single-qubit rotations)                       │
│                          │ - Two layers of CRZ gates: one on adjacent pairs (0-1, 2-3, 4-5, 6-7) and one on wider    │
│                          │ pairs (1-3, 3-5, 5-7)                                                                     │
│                          │ - Shared final RZ (parameter reuse across qubits)                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This design captures necessary two-qubit correlations with minimal redundancy, achieving  │
│                          │ 98 parameters and validation loss of 0.03.                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current multi-layer approach (CRX, CRY, CRZ long-range, and independent RY final)     │
│                          │ creates too many independent parameters that compete during training, hurting             │
│                          │ generalization.                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Recommendation: Replace the current ansatz with the proven simpler pattern from the       │
│                          │ second program. This restores parameter efficiency and validation performance while       │
│                          │ maintaining accuracy.                                                                     │
