│ patch_description        │ This edit replaces the current high-parameter mixed-axis block with a more structured and │
│                          │ parameter-efficient ansatz.                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key changes:                                                                              │
│                          │ - Preserve per-qubit input expressivity with one RY on each qubit.                        │
│                          │ - Replace the heavier CRX/CRY/CRZ stack with a cleaner CRZ entangling scaffold.           │
│                          │ - Add a sparse long-range skip link, `CRZ(0,4)`, to help the circuit capture non-local    │
│                          │ correlations without much overhead.                                                       │
│                          │ - Replace the final per-qubit RY layer with a single shared RY mixer applied to all       │
│                          │ qubits, which keeps the output layer trainable while reducing parameter count and helping │
│                          │ regularization.                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should improve optimization stability, lower the train-test gap, and reduce L2 loss  │
│                          │ while using parameters more efficiently.                                                  │
